Task 2.3: Synthesis voices (Red + Green)

What: src/audio/voices.ts - six voice specs as pure data (pluck:
fast triangle music box; pad: slow-swell sine, low-passed; arpeggio:
tamed square staccato; shimmer: noise band via looped white-noise
buffer, high low-pass; percussion: near-instant strike; marimba:
soft sine) plus envelopeFor(), a pure envelope function that clamps
attack+release to fit any note duration (short notes shrink
proportionally, hold goes to zero, never negative). sound.ts
musicHost now routes every scheduled note through its voice spec:
oscillator or noise source, envelope gain, optional low-pass filter,
into the theme bus. SFX (tone()) untouched; call sites unchanged.

Tests: 10 voices cases written first (Red: unresolved module) -
spec existence for all six names, unknown-name fallback to pluck,
per-voice character assertions (fast pluck, slow pad, noise shimmer,
instant percussion), envelope natural/clamped/near-zero cases; 2
wiring cases in sound.test.ts (shimmer note -> buffer source not
oscillator; pluck note -> oscillator); StubAudioContext extended
with sampleRate, createBufferSource, createBuffer, createBiquadFilter.
Whole unit suite: 191/191. voices.ts coverage 100% across the board.

Why: per-screen moods need distinct timbres; keeping voices pure
lets compositions be tuned as data and keeps the WebAudio wiring thin.

